column6:
The project will be established on the newly acquired lot in Balilihan, Bohol, with an area of 6 hectares. The proposed project aims to enhance the tourism and sports training center in the province of Bohol. It will play a major role in providing professional and technological tourism and sports instruction that addresses the community's demands. The outputs of the project include the following:
a) Ground Development and Utilities (fully developed and landscaped 6-hectare project site);
b) Academic and Training Facilities which include a 5-storey Tourism Institute Building, two 3-storey classroom buildings, 3-storey laboratory building, 2-storey training center, and 3-storey testing center;
c) Sports facilities, which include a 5-storey sports laboratory, track and field oval, aqua hub, open game court facilities, bleachers, and stage;
d) Community and Student-Focused Spaces.
